---
// ABOUT: the letter (artifact "Three Homepages", Version C) inside Version E's
// frame. Decided by Jamie 9 Sep 2026 (doc 71 §6). The homepage's "Heard of
// Jamie? Tell me more before I decide" exit lands here, so the page is a
// piece of writing, not a bio. Paper column for the letter; E's proof band and
// final CTA close it out. Every line was read and owned by Jamie.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import StickyBook from '../components/StickyBook.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { REVIEWS, GOOGLE_RATING, REVIEWS_URL } from '../data/reviews';
import '@fontsource/source-serif-4/400.css';
import '@fontsource/source-serif-4/400-italic.css';
import '@fontsource/source-serif-4/600.css';

import assess from '../assets/home/door-hurt.jpg';
import hinge from '../assets/home/door-muscle.jpg';
import portraitMural from '../assets/about/portrait-mural.jpg';

const title = 'About Jamie Atlas, Personal Trainer & Rehab Specialist, Denver';
const description =
  "Named 5280's Best Personal Trainer in Denver three times. BSc Neuroscience (ANU), CFT, FAFS, NSCA-CSCS, NASM-CPT, Cert IV Nutrition Coaching. 25 years training Denver, in one basement on Glenarm Place since 2010.";

// Two pull-quotes: Marcus (return to sport) and Susan (strength over 60).
const pulls = REVIEWS.filter(r => r.name === 'Marcus Kret' || r.name === 'Susan Keicher');

const personSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  '@id': `${SITE.url}/#jamie`, // same node as BaseLayout's founder, one entity
  name: 'Jamie Atlas',
  jobTitle: 'Personal Trainer & Rehab Specialist',
  award: [...SITE.awards],
  worksFor: { '@id': SITE.url },
  url: `${SITE.url}/about`,
  email: SITE.contact.email,
  telephone: SITE.contact.phone,
  image: new URL('/jamie-portrait.jpg', Astro.site).href,
  sameAs: [SITE.social.instagramUrl],
  knowsAbout: ['Personal training', 'Strength and conditioning', 'Return-to-sport training', 'Cognitive Functional Therapy', 'Applied Functional Science', 'Nutrition coaching'],
  hasCredential: SITE.credentials.map(c => ({
    '@type': 'EducationalOccupationalCredential',
    name: c.name,
  })),
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} image="/jamie-portrait.jpg">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(personSchema)} />

  <div class="about-e">

    <!-- E-frame strip: answers the exit link that brought most people here -->
    <section class="strip">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6 py-8 sm:py-10">
        <p class="who"><b>Jamie Atlas</b> · Personal Trainer &amp; Rehab Specialist · {SITE.contact.address.street}, downtown Denver</p>
        <p class="greet">You asked to hear more before deciding. Fair.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- THE LETTER -->
    <article class="paper">
      <div class="col">
        <h1>For about fifteen years I told people to work around the sore bit. I'd like that on the record before we go any further.</h1>

        <p class="lead">
          Every personal trainer in Denver will happily train around your bad knee. I did it too, and I had slides.
          Then I spent the better part of a decade learning why the knee keeps coming back into the conversation, and
          the short version is this: the knee is usually the messenger.
        </p>

        <p class="line">Where it hurts and why it hurts are often two different places.</p>

        <p>
          So here is what I do now, in a basement on Glenarm Place, one person at a time. I train you for the thing you
          want to do. Ski, golf, run, lift, carry a grandchild up the stairs. And I keep one eye on the joint you're
          worried about the whole time. Nutrition coaching comes with it. So does the rehab work. Nobody sends you down
          the hall to somebody else.
        </p>

        <p class="cred">
          <span><b>{SITE.awardBadge}</b></span>
          <span>9NEWS fitness expert</span>
          <span>25 years training Denver</span>
          <span>{GOOGLE_RATING.stars.toFixed(1)} on Google, {GOOGLE_RATING.count} reviews</span>
        </p>

        <figure>
          <Image src={assess} alt="Jamie Atlas, personal trainer, kneeling to assess a client's ankle on a balance board at his downtown Denver studio" widths={[640, 1100]} sizes="(min-width: 700px) 640px, 100vw" format="webp" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption><i>This is me looking at an ankle as if it owes me money. It usually does.</i></figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h2>Three kinds of people walk in here</h2>
        <p>Most of them have already been somewhere else. Often several somewheres. See if one of these is you.</p>

        <div class="doors">
          <div class="door lead-door">
            <b>You want to get better at your sport without getting hurt again.</b>
            <p>This is most of what I do. Training built around the joint, with someone watching it. <a href="/this-is-you/worried-about-reinjury">Read more →</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="door">
            <b>You're hurt and you want to get better.</b>
            <p>The PT, the chiro, the injections. The system sometimes lets people down, and where it drops off is where we begin. <a href="/this-is-you/still-in-pain">Read more →</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="door">
            <b>You want to lose the weight and keep the muscle.</b>
            <p>On a GLP-1 or not. Strength first, so what comes off is fat and what stays is you. <a href="/personal-trainer-denver/glp-1">Read more →</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <figure class="narrow">
          <Image src={hinge} alt="A client in his sixties hinging with a kettlebell in front of the mural at Jamie Atlas's Denver studio" widths={[420, 840]} sizes="420px" format="webp" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption><i>Sixty is a perfectly good age to get strong. I have the clients to prove it.</i></figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h2>What I'm bad at</h2>
        <p>
          Here's a question nobody asks a trainer and everybody should: what are you bad at? For years I'd have
          answered that with something slippery. "Well, it depends on the person!" True, and also the single most
          useless sentence in my industry.
        </p>
        <p>
          So. The unflattering half. This is not urgent care and it is not a diagnosis; a small number of things that
          hurt need a doctor before they need me, and I'll say so in the first thirty minutes. If what you want is
          hands on you for an hour, I'm the wrong room, and I can name three people who are the right one. And if you
          want someone to count reps at you, the ab roller did that for $19.95 in 1994 and it didn't work then either.
        </p>

        <h2>The first thirty minutes</h2>
        <p>
          An assessment, {SITE.pricing.firstVisit}, in the studio or on Zoom. Your story, a look at how you move, one
          change you can measure before you leave, and my plain read on whether I can help. Ongoing sessions are
          {SITE.pricing.session60} for sixty minutes or {SITE.pricing.session30} for thirty, one-on-one, every time.
          The 6:30am and 5:15pm slots are open most weeks.
        </p>

        <div class="pull">
          {pulls.map(r => (
            <blockquote>
              <span class="stars" aria-label="Five stars">★★★★★</span>
              "{r.text}"
              <footer>{r.name}, <a href={REVIEWS_URL} rel="noopener">on Google</a></footer>
            </blockquote>
          ))}
        </div>

        <p>
          5280 magazine has handed this basement six 5280 Top of the Town awards and the Denver A-List two more, which
          is eight more awards than I've won for anything else.
        </p>
        <p>
          The rest of the CV, briefly: BSc Neuroscience from the Australian National University, Cognitive Functional
          Therapy, Applied Functional Science at the Gray Institute, NSCA-CSCS, NASM-CPT, a Certificate IV in Nutrition
          Coaching, the 9NEWS fitness expert, and 25 years training Denver, including a few UFC, NFL, NBA and NHL
          athletes I'm not allowed to name and a great many Coloradans who just wanted their knee back.
        </p>

        <figure>
          <Image src={portraitMural} alt="Jamie Atlas, personal trainer and rehab specialist, arms crossed in front of the mural at his downtown Denver studio" widths={[640, 1100, 1600]} sizes="(min-width: 700px) 640px, 100vw" format="webp" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption><i>Pictured: the reason the pseudonyms in my case studies never hold up.</i></figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p>
          Read that back and it's fairly obvious, isn't it. The sore bit is where the argument ends up, rarely where it
          starts. Which makes it a bit odd that the whole industry trains around it, and odder still that I did too,
          for fifteen years, with confidence.
        </p>

        <p class="line joke">So there you have it.</p>

        <hr class="rule" />

        <div class="cta">
          <p>Thirty-minute assessment, {SITE.pricing.firstVisit}. Your story, my read on whether I can help, and if I can't, the name of who can.</p>
          <a href="/book" class="cta-button">Book a 30-minute assessment</a>
          <small>{SITE.contact.address.street}, {SITE.contact.address.level}, {SITE.contact.address.city} {SITE.contact.address.zip} · <a href={`tel:${SITE.contact.phoneTel}`}>{SITE.contact.phone}</a> · or on Zoom</small>
        </div>

        <p class="sig">Yours in health,<br />Jamie Atlas</p>

        <p class="ps"><b>PS</b> The 6:30am crowd are a particular kind of person and I like them very much.</p>
        <p class="ps"><b>PPS</b> If you're on Ozempic, Wegovy or Mounjaro and worried about losing muscle along with the weight, there's a page for exactly that. <a href="/personal-trainer-denver/glp-1">Here it is.</a></p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- CREDENTIALS + MEDIA -->
    <section class="lists">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-14 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-10">
        <div>
          <h3>Credentials</h3>
          <ul>
            {SITE.credentials.map(c => <li>{c.name}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Seen in &amp; contributed to</h3>
          <ul>
            {SITE.media.map(m => <li>{m.label}</li>)}
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm"><a href="/press">Press and the award years, in full →</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- E PROOF BAND -->
    <div class="proof">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4">
        <div><b>6×</b><span>5280 Top of the Town winner</span></div>
        <div><b>2×</b><span>Denver A-List winner</span></div>
        <div><b>9NEWS</b><span>The station's fitness expert · 25 years training Denver</span></div>
        <div><b>{GOOGLE_RATING.stars.toFixed(1)}</b><span>Google rating, {GOOGLE_RATING.count} reviews, all verbatim</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- E FINAL CTA -->
    <section class="final">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6 py-16 sm:py-20 text-center">
        <h2>Thirty minutes. One measurable change. Then you decide.</h2>
        <p>
          A 30-minute assessment, {SITE.pricing.firstVisit}, in the studio or on Zoom. If it's not a fit I'll say so in the first half hour,
          and I'll know who is.
        </p>
        <a href="/book" class="cta-button text-lg">Book a 30-minute assessment</a>
        <p class="nap">
          {SITE.contact.address.street}, {SITE.contact.address.level} · <a href={`tel:${SITE.contact.phoneTel}`}>{SITE.contact.phone}</a> · Mon to Fri {SITE.hours.weekdays} · Sat {SITE.hours.saturday}
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>

  <StickyBook />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-e {
    --navy: #0b1620;
    --deep: #0b2e45;
    --blue: #0079c2;
    --sky: #7cc4f0;
    --orange: #f5921e;
    --red: #b91d2b;
    --paper: #fbfbf9;
    --ink: #1f2933;
  }

  /* strip */
  .strip { background: var(--navy); color: #fff; }
  .who { font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--sky); margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .who b { color: #fff; }
  .greet { font-family: 'Barlow Semi Condensed', 'Inter', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px); line-height: 1; color: #fff; text-wrap: balance; margin: 0; }

  /* the letter */
  .paper { background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font-family: 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.62; padding: 48px 20px 40px; }
  .paper .col { max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .paper h1 { font-family: 'Quicksand', 'Inter', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 42px); line-height: 1.18; color: var(--deep); margin: 0 0 26px; text-wrap: balance; }
  .paper h2 { font-family: 'Quicksand', 'Inter', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(20px, 2.6vw, 26px); letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--deep); margin: 44px 0 16px; }
  .paper p { margin: 0 0 20px; }
  .paper p.lead { font-size: 21px; }
  .paper .line { font-family: 'Quicksand', 'Inter', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 30px); line-height: 1.25; color: var(--blue); margin: 36px 0; text-wrap: balance; }
  .paper .line.joke { color: var(--deep); font-weight: 600; font-style: italic; font-family: 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif; font-size: clamp(20px, 2.6vw, 25px); }
  .paper figure { margin: 36px 0; }
  .paper figure.narrow { max-width: 420px; }
  .paper figure img { border-radius: 6px; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .paper figcaption { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 14px; color: #5b6b7a; margin-top: 10px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .paper figcaption i { color: var(--deep); font-style: italic; font-family: 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif; font-size: 16px; }
  .paper .cred { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 14.5px; color: #3d4b58; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 18px; margin: 8px 0 8px; }
  .paper .cred b { color: var(--red); }
  .paper .doors { display: grid; gap: 14px; margin: 8px 0 12px; }
  .paper .door { border-left: 3px solid var(--blue); padding: 6px 0 6px 18px; }
  .paper .door.lead-door { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .paper .door b { font-family: 'Quicksand', 'Inter', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; color: var(--deep); display: block; font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .paper .door p { margin: 0; font-size: 18px; }
  .paper .door a { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--blue); text-decoration: none; }
  .paper .pull { border-top: 1px solid #d9e1e8; border-bottom: 1px solid #d9e1e8; padding: 22px 0 8px; margin: 36px 0; }
  .paper .pull blockquote { margin: 0 0 14px; font-size: 18px; font-style: italic; }
  .paper .pull blockquote footer { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-size: 13.5px; color: #5b6b7a; margin-top: 4px; }
  .paper .stars { color: var(--orange); letter-spacing: 2px; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; display: block; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .paper .rule { border: 0; border-top: 2px solid var(--deep); width: 88px; margin: 40px 0 24px; }
  .paper .cta { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; background: #ecf6fd; border-radius: 10px; padding: 22px 24px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .paper .cta p { font-size: 16.5px; margin-bottom: 14px; color: var(--ink); }
  .paper .cta small { display: block; color: #5b6b7a; font-size: 13.5px; margin-top: 12px; }
  .paper .sig { font-family: 'Quicksand', 'Inter', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; color: var(--deep); font-size: 20px; margin-top: 30px; }
  .paper .ps { font-size: 17px; color: #3d4b58; }
  .paper .ps b { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: .08em; color: var(--blue); margin-right: 8px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .paper { font-size: 17.5px; } .paper p.lead { font-size: 19px; } }

  /* credentials */
  .lists { background: #fff; border-top: 1px solid #e1e8ee; }
  .lists h3 { font-family: 'Quicksand', 'Inter', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: 20px; color: var(--deep); margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .lists ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .lists li { padding: 6px 0; border-top: 1px solid #e1e8ee; font-size: 15.5px; color: #3d4b58; }

  /* proof band (same as the homepage) */
  .proof { background: var(--blue); color: #fff; }
  .proof > div > div { padding: 22px 18px; border-right: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.22); }
  .proof > div > div:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .proof b { display: block; font-family: 'Barlow Semi Condensed', 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 34px; line-height: 1; font-weight: 800; }
  .proof span { display: block; font-size: 13.5px; color: #d5ebfa; margin-top: 6px; }

  /* final (same as the homepage) */
  .final { background: #fff; color: var(--navy); }
  .final h2 { font-family: 'Barlow Semi Condensed', 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: clamp(30px, 4.4vw, 52px); line-height: 1; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .final p { color: #3d4b58; font-size: 18px; max-width: 54ch; margin: 0 auto 24px; }
  .final .nap { font-size: 14.5px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--deep); margin-top: 22px; }
  .final .nap a { color: var(--deep); }
</style>
